  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ansari Sahidkha Salimkha vs The Chief Officer on 11 March, 2024 Author: Vaibhavi D. Nanavati Bench: Vaibhavi D. Nanavati Neutral C C/Sca/900/2024 Order DATED: 11/03/2024 undefine IN THE HIGH COURT OF GUJARAT AT AHMEDABAD R/SPECIAL CIVIL APPLICATION NO. 900 of 2024 ========================================================== ANSARI SAHIDKHA SALIMKHA Versus THE CHIEF OFFICER ========================================================== Appearance: NABIL O BLOCH(7953) for the Petitioner(s) No. 1 MR CHIRAG B PATEL(3679) for the Respondent(s) No. 1 ========================================================== CORAM:HONOURABLE MS. JUSTICE VAIBHAVI D. NANAVATI Date : 11/03/2024 ORAL ORDER 1. By way of present writ-application filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of India the writ-applicant herein has prayed for the following reliefs :- \"(A) Direct the Respondent -The Chief Officer - Sahera Nagar Palika to process the application filed by the Petitioner at Annexure A to this Petition and Grant a Legal and Valid NOC and Permission for Running Slaughter expeditiously without booking any delay as Petitioner is identical situated as Order as CAV order dated 11.4.2023 passed in CA NO 10 OF 2023 IN WRIT PETITION (PIL) No. 133 of 2021 by this Honorable Court Annexure-B and and SCA No.17141 of 2023 order (B) Direct the Ansari Sahidkha Salimkha vs The Chief Officer on 11 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/170081359/ 1 Respondent -The Chief Officer - Sahera Nagar NEUTRAL CITATION C/SCA/900/2024 ORDER DATED: 11/03/2024 undefined Palika to process the application filed by the Petitioner at Annexure A to this Petition and to give opportunity of hearing to Grant a Legal and Valid NOC and Permission for Running Slaughter and (B) grant any other relief or pass any other order, which the Honourable Court may consider just and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case and in the interest of justice.\"",
    "facts": "It is the case of the writ-applicant that by way of present writ-application the writ-applicant herein seeks direction to provide legal and valid NOC and permission for running slaughter house under the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 for licensing and registration of food business.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Patel, the learned advocate appearing for the respondent authority submitted that the respondent authority would consider if such an application is filed in line with the order dated 11.4.2023 passed in the Civil Application No.10 of 2023 in Writ Petition (PIL) No.133 of 2021."
  },
